      "writtenOn": "2018-03-14T21:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was the recommendation from Aaron to include baseboard.h for the boards that use it. I had a test-only CL which included where Vincent suggests. If it\u0027s included here then the Makefile doesn\u0027t need HAS_BASEBOARD. I did test with moving a section of config options to baseboard.h and it builds fine. When I move #include \"baseboard.h\" to config.h and make it conditional on a CPPFLAG I added \u0027HAS_BASEBOARD\u0027 then it had build errors with some of the config options I had moved to baseboard.h. When it\u0027s included unconditionally, then I don\u0027t see those errors.",
